# Graphify × Fast CLI (gated)

**Gate:** If `graphify-out/graph.json` is missing → normal `rg`/`fd`/`ast-grep` only. Do not call graphify, MCP graph tools, or `/graphify`.

When the gate passes:

```text
L0 MCP (only if tools exist) → L1 graphify query|path|explain --budget 1500
→ L2 scoped rg/fd/ast-grep → L3 edit (replace_file_content/sd) → L4 graphify update . (once per edit batch)
```

- **Task Routing**:
  - **Survey / Doc / Architecture Audit**: Mandatory `just test` (for instant 80+ ground-truth checks) + L0/L1 first (do NOT bypass just because a single doc file is named in prompt).
  - **Pinpoint Fix**: Bypass L0/L1 directly to L2 (`rg -n`).
- **Two-Tier Discovery & Strict Budget**: Tier 1 (Topology via L0/L1) → Tier 2 (Granular values via `rg -n` only on scoped files). Max 2–3 `view_file` calls per task. Never read 4+ whole files sequentially.
- Cursor often has no graphify MCP → default L1 (`graphify query "<q>" --budget 1500`); never retry-loop missing tools.
- **L4 Sync**: Run `graphify update .` once at end of a coherent edit batch (not after every file). Skip if graph was absent.
- Never run full multimodal `/graphify .` unless the user asks.
- Prefer scoped subgraph / wiki over `GRAPH_REPORT.md` or multi-file reads.

